            <title>[LU-21050] fix length check in cfs_abs_path()</title>
                <link>https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-21050</link>
                <project id="10000" key="LU">Lustre</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;When cfs_abs_path() appends the file name to the resolved parent&lt;br/&gt;
directory, it stores the snprintf() result in "len", which already&lt;br/&gt;
holds the length of the parent. The overflow check that follows,&lt;br/&gt;
"len &amp;gt;= sizeof(buf) - len", then compares the appended length against&lt;br/&gt;
the wrong remaining space. Truncation is only detected when the file&lt;br/&gt;
name alone is longer than about half of the buffer, so a long parent&lt;br/&gt;
path combined with a long file name can be silently truncated.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Keep the snprintf() result in a separate variable and compare it&lt;br/&gt;
against the space left after the parent, sizeof(buf) - len. Also treat&lt;br/&gt;
a negative return as an error, and cast the result to size_t for the&lt;br/&gt;
comparison so that it is never converted from a negative value.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;This is unlikely to be hit in practice because it needs a path close to&lt;br/&gt;
PATH_MAX, but a truncated path should be reported as -ENAMETOOLONG&lt;br/&gt;
instead of being returned to the caller.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
